            "Saurav Nanda",
            "Ganapathy Parthasarathy",
            "Bhuvnesh Kumar",
            "Parivesh Choudhary"
          ],
          "summary": "Direct Nash Optimization (DNO) aligns a language model to a general preference function by approximating the Nash equilibrium of a two-player preference game. Its practical variant, DNO-Prct, iterates on-policy sampling, LLM-based rating of the samples together with a teacher's gold response, large-margin preference-pair selection and a DPO-style contrastive update. We re-implement DNO-Prct independently and study it on two open-weight instruct models, Llama 3.1 8B Instruct and Mistral 7B Instru"
        },
        {
